From: PwndaWallet swap sidecar
Date: 2026-09-03
Subject: [PATCH 16/19] basicswap: register ZANO (Coins.ZANO = 16)

Wires PWNDA-PATCH-15's Zano module into the engine's shared registries:
`chainparams.py` (uncomments upstream's OWN reserved `ZANO = 16` slot rather
than renumbering, adds `zano_params`, and joins `scriptless_coins` and
`xmr_based_coins`), `basicswap.py` (a `createInterface` branch, a
`thread_func` entry, the allow-list copies for `walletrpcjwt` /
`scratchwalletrpcport` / `scratchwalletrpcjwt` / `external_main_wallet`
beside PWNDA-PATCH-8's own `mainwalletrpc*` hunk, and a ZANO-specific
`getTotalBalance` branch), and `bin/prepare.py` (`coin_prepare_modules` and
`known_coins`).

Three real defects were fixed here beyond a literal port of REU26's own
registration: REU26's allow-list hunk leaves `walletrpcpassword` mandatory,
which breaks Grove's JWT-only ZANO; `external_main_wallet` reached no
allow-list at all, so PWNDA-PATCH-15's flag could only ever read False; and
`getTotalBalance` called `get_balance` where Zano's method is `getbalance`
(REU26's own documented rung 5-6 bug, silently swallowed by an except-fallback).

RECONSTRUCTED 2026-09-03: this file was lost from `upstream/patches/` by an
orchestrating-session mistake (moved aside during an abandoned experiment, then
deleted with the scratch directory that held it). The patch BODY below was
regenerated by diffing two verified trees and the full series was re-validated
end to end afterwards; the body is byte-exact. This header prose is rewritten
from `upstream/patches/README.md`, `PwndaWalletVault/log.md`, and the code
itself -- accurate, but not the original wording. See log.md 2026-09-03
"patch-series recovery".

Rebased 2026-09-08 for basicswap v0.18.6 (ea39faddbcaf). Context only:
upstream 9bf06570 appended "electrum_poll_interval" to the same
chain_client_settings passthrough tuple this patch appends
"external_main_wallet" to, so hunk 1 no longer matched. Both entries now
sit in the tuple; nothing about the ZANO wallet-rpc work changed.

